  ('group', 'csikzsuzsi@gmail.com', 'Zsuzsa Csik', 'Hi, sorry I''m a bit late to the party but the week was busy!
I''m from Hungary but currently living in Brazil. I learned to play the piano between the ages of 6 and 12, when adolescence took over and I quit. I regretted it soon after, yet it took 27 years to pick it up again. I finally got a Roland FP-30x in late January this year, and I love starting over.
Interestingly, I don''t know how, but 6-year-old me made a weird deal with my piano teacher, so I hardly learned any music theory beyond the bare minimum to read the notes. No scales, no chords, nothing like that. Now I''m catching up with all that.
I don''t have any particular goals other than having fun and learning nice pieces. I started with some recommendations, I think from Matt''s videos (Menuet in F, Menuet in G), and now I''m trying the Clementi Sonatina. Soon, I will gather my courage and record something to get my first feedback, as I don''t have a teacher.
